## Notes before you ship

- **[P1] Pre-compute aggregates.** Add something like `Map<String, Object> stats` (counts, sums, min/max per group) and include it in the prompt as `<facts>`. Tell the model to quote those numbers rather than derive them.
- **[P1] Async for long jobs.** A 2000-record map-reduce can take several minutes, which exceeds typical gateway or proxy timeouts. Return `202` with a job ID, or stream the final step with `chatClient.prompt()...stream().content()`. If this runs behind your WebFlux gateway, the streaming route is the natural fit.
- **[P2] Observability.** Spring AI emits Micrometer metrics for model calls. Log chunk count and total chars per request so you can tune `chunk-chars`.
- **[P2] If one chunk works for you.** With `num-ctx` raised to 64k+ and compacted JSON under about 100k chars, single-pass is simpler and keeps cross-record context. Map-reduce can miss relationships between records in different chunks, so test both on real data.

